NBA Trivia (20-0) — sources & licences

Design    Built from the "20-0 v2" screens of the "Mobile app design decisions" design project, refreshed in 2026:
          dark rounded cards, a colour per difficulty level, team colours on the three-letter marks, a four-tab
          menu (sidebar on desktop). Styles in app.css; modernist.css supplies the base reset and form controls.
Code      index.html (screen markup + icon set), app.js (screen logic), dc.js (renderer). Question bank and engine
          in data/ (engine.js, questions.js, mystery.js, teams.js, facts.js).
Fonts     Archivo (The Archivo Project Authors / Omnibus-Type) and, for Arabic, Cairo (The Cairo Project Authors),
          both SIL Open Font License 1.1; files and licences in fonts/.
Languages English and Arabic: i18n/en.json and i18n/ar.json (i18next format), loaded by i18n.js.
Images    None. Icons are drawn inline (index.html). No team or league logos are used; teams appear as three-letter
          text marks in the team's colour.
Data      NBA facts are used for trivia reference only.
          - Games, teams and players: balldontlie (balldontlie.io), 1946-47 to the present.
          - Missing and corrected game scores, played dates of postponed games, team box scores,
            draft history and player bios: "NBA Database" by Wyatt Walsh,
            https://www.kaggle.com/datasets/wyattowalsh/basketball, licensed CC BY-SA 4.0
            (data from stats.nba.com). Questions built from it carry the same licence.
          - The two are merged by tools/merge.mjs; tools/DATA.md lists what each one lacked.
          - Awards table and jersey numbers: hand-checked.
          Accounts, stats, leaderboards and head-to-head live in Supabase (supabase/migrations);
          guests and offline play fall back to the device. supabase-js 2.118.0 (MIT) is vendored in vendor/.

Live      https://nba-trivia-20-0.netlify.app (Netlify project nba-trivia-20-0; data in Supabase).
Run       Serve this folder over HTTP (ES modules don't load from file://), e.g.  python3 -m http.server  and open
          index.html.
